    "title": "LA County sheriff's motorcycle deputy injured during training accident in Santa Clarita - NewsBreak",
    "text": "9 hours ago\nA Los Angeles County sheriff's motorcycle deputy was injured Wednesday morning after being involved in a training accident in Santa Clarita.\nThe crash was reported just after 10:30 a.m. near San Francisquito Canyon Road and Copper Hill Drive.\nVideo from AIR7 showed the motorcycle on the side of the road.\nIt's unclear what led to the crash. According to an update from the sheriff's department, the deputy suffered only minor injuries.\nThe incident remains under investigation.\nThis is a developing story. This article will continue to be updated as more information becomes available.",
    "summary": "A Los Angeles County sheriff's motorcycle deputy was injured Wednesday morning after being involved in a training accident in Santa Clarita. The crash was reported just after 10:30 a.m. near San Francisquito Canyon Road and Copper Hill Drive. Video from AIR7 showed the motorcycle on the side of the road. According to an update from the sheriff's department, the deputy suffered only minor injuries. This article will continue to be updated as more information becomes available.",
